{"Title":"An Act authorizing raising the maximum retirement age of special police officers in the city of Methuen to 70 years old","BillNumber":"H4895","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"J23","Name":"Joint Committee on Public Service","Type":2,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J23","ResponseDate":"2024-07-22T13:10:42.493"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"RMH2","Name":"Ryan M. Hamilton","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/RMH2","ResponseDate":"2024-03-14T12:49:56.7166667"},{"Id":"EAR1","Name":"Estela A. Reyes","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/EAR1","ResponseDate":"2024-03-14T13:10:41.0766667"},{"Id":"FEP1","Name":"Francisco E. Paulino","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/FEP1","ResponseDate":"2024-04-08T18:52:41.43"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H4895/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":null,"DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. The mayor of the City of Methuen may, if the mayor deems necessary following the recommendation of the Chief of Police, appoint individuals, who have served as police officers and who are currently certified by Peace Officer Standards and Training (POST) Commission, to serve as special police officers for the purpose of performing traffic details.\r\n\tSECTION 2. Notwithstanding section 1 of chapter 32 of the General Laws or any other general or special law to the contrary, the maximum age for a special police officer appointed in the City of Methuen shall be 70 years of age. \r\n\tSECTION 3. Special police officers who are between the ages of 65-70 years of age shall only perform traffic details in the City of Methuen. \r\n\tSECTION. 4. No further deductions shall be made from the regular compensation of any individual over the age of 65 appointed pursuant to this Act under chapter 32 of the General Laws and, upon retirement, said individuals appointed pursuant to this Act shall receive a superannuation retirement allowance equal to the allowance to which he would have been entitled had he retired upon reaching the age of 65.\r\n\tSECTION 5. This act shall take effect upon passage.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Redraft","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J23","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J23"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Place in OD","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"H52","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/H52"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Correctly Drawn","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"H36","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/H36"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[{"AmendmentNumber":"1","ParentBillNumber":"H4895","Branch":"House","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H4895/Branches/House/Amendments/1/"}]}